course: dictionary
lesson: 3516
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Fault is a good example. It can mean a mistake you caused, a weak spot in someone's character, a problem in a machine, a crack in the ground, or a bad serve in tennis. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «A fault is a crack in the Earth's crust where rocks can slip.» The words crust and rocks are the clues. They show that fault means a crack in the ground here, not a mistake. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the words around it?
explain: «It's not your fault» is about blame. It means you did not cause the problem. To check, swap in your meaning: "it's not your mistake" still makes sense, so you have got it right.
explain: «A hot plug or socket, or a smell of burning, means an electrical fault.» Here fault means a problem in a machine or its wiring. The context also tells you what to do: switch off if it is safe and tell a grown-up at once.
fact: Fault can be a noun (a fault, faults) or a verb (fault, faults, faulted, faulting).
fact: «My fault» means I caused the mistake or the bad thing, and saying sorry for it is honest.
fact: «At fault» means responsible for something bad.
fact: «Find fault with» means to complain about something.
fact: In science, a fault is a crack in the Earth's crust where rocks move. Earthquakes happen along faults, like the San Andreas Fault in California.
exercise: «The vase broke, and Sam said, "It was my fault."» What does fault mean here? | *The mistake was caused by Sam | A bad serve in tennis | A weak spot in a machine | A crack in the ground
exercise: «The lights flickered because of an electrical fault.» What is the fault? | *A problem in the wiring or a machine | A rule that everyone must follow | Something Sam did on purpose | A crack in the rocks under the ground
exercise: In tennis, a fault is a bad serve. Which sentence uses fault this way? | The engine had a fault and would not start | Her only fault is that she is late | *The player's first serve was a fault, so she got a second try | The earthquake split the fault wide open
test: «His only fault is that he is late.» What does fault mean? | *A weak or bad part of someone's character | A crack in the ground | A problem with a machine | A bad serve in tennis
test: Which phrase means you are responsible for something bad? | a bad serve | electrical fault | find fault with | *at fault
exam: «It's not your fault» means what? | You caused the problem and must say sorry | *You did not cause the problem | The machine is broken and needs fixing | You must pay for the damage
